% Generate pdd/commands/auth.py for self-hosted bearer-token configuration.

Export auth_group, a Click group named auth. Use CloudConfig and httpx.
login verifies credentials with GET listSessions on the configured URL, timeout 10 seconds.
Require URL plus token. Explain PDD_CLOUD_URL and PDD_CLOUD_TOKEN or PDD_CLOUD_TOKEN_FILE when missing.
Accept --browser/--no-browser for compatibility; neither opens a browser.
status reports local mode when unconfigured and otherwise reports the URL and token availability.
Only status --verify contacts the service. HTTP rejection or network failure exits with an error.
Never print the token during status or verification.
logout explains unsetting client credentials, restarting connect, and revoking tokens on the server.
clear-cache explains that bearer authentication has no token cache.
Neither command deletes identity caches or changes another process's environment.
token explicitly exports the configured token; support --format raw|json.
JSON output contains token. Missing credentials cause an error.
Do not use Firebase, GitHub device flow, keyring, or auth_service.
